-Some terminals accept similar sequences, with semicolons replaced by colons
-and an extra colon after the number 2 (this is conformant to the ISO 8613-6
-standard, but less widely supported): >
+Some terminals accept similar sequences for |t_8f| and |t_8b|, with semicolons
+replaced by colons and an extra colon after the number 2 (this is conformant
+to the ISO 8613-6 standard, but less widely supported): >
 	 let &t_8f = "\<Esc>[38:2::%lu:%lu:%lum"
 	 let &t_8b = "\<Esc>[48:2::%lu:%lu:%lum"
-	 let &t_8u = "\<Esc>[58:2::%lu:%lu:%lum"
+
+For the color of underline and undercurl (|t_8u| and |t_AU|) the colon form is
+used.  Terminals that support the underline color should accept it some even
+require it.  In a terminal without support for the underline color, such
+as xterm, the underline keeps the text color and other attributes stay as
+they are.
 
